    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0069" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8890/973¹⁄₆: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-27T18:00:00-04:00">October 27, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. … as mentioned in your 47 of August 5 and related telegrams, the Department
                    has been endeavoring to provide means for bringing to the United States the
                    items mentioned in your 48 of the same date, together with additional quantity
                    of wool regarding which the Afghan Consul at New York has requested the
                    Department’s assistance.</p>
                <p>The British Embassy at Washington suggests that the assistance which the
                    Department is endeavoring to render is not warranted, maintaining that the
                    majority of 1941 Afghan lambskins are now unsold in the United States, that
                    those skins the movement of which the Department is endeavoring to effect
                    constitute only an insignificant quantity, and that with regard to wool and
                    pistachio nuts, India and Russia are the normal markets. …</p>
                <p>The Department remains of the opinion that from the point of view of this country
                    the assistance recommended by you in your telegrams under reference should be
                    accorded if possible. However, … your comments on the subject are urgently
                    requested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
